<title>USA: U.S. Stockpile sells zinc for avg $0.4768/lb.</title>
<headline>U.S. Stockpile sells zinc for avg $0.4768/lb.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Defense National Stockpile Center said Tuesday it sold 6,014,000 pounds of surplus zinc for an average $0.4768 per pound.  </p>
<p>Sales were as follows, in lbs and $/lb:</p>
<p>    Tally Metals	  225,000  0.4881</p>
<p>    Tally Metals	   45,000  0.4873</p>
<p>Hochschild Partners 880,000  0.4790</p>
<p>    Sogem Afrimet	 660,000  0.4782</p>
<p>    Sogem Afrimet	 660,000  0.4762</p>
<p>    Sogem Afrimet	 660,000  0.4742</p>
<p>    Sogem Afrimet	 660,000  0.4732</p>
<p>    Commercial Alloys   640,000  0.4780</p>
<p>Colwell Kennedy,</p>
<p>		Australia   660,000  0.4770</p>
<p>Colwell Kennedy,</p>
<p>		Australia   660,000  0.4745</p>
<p>    Trademet		264,000  0.4737</p>
<p>-- Washington Commodities Desk (202) 898-8489</p>
</text>
